/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1354760211/10/des.md:163:- The grid (15x15 to 25x25) contains several arrow-shaped objects, each in a distinct non-black color. Each arrow consists of a straight body segment (horizontal or vertical, at least 2 pixels long and at most 5) plus a one-pixel arrowhead that branches from one end of the body in a perpendicular direction, indicating the arrow's pointing direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1354760211/10/des.md:164:  - For a horizontal body, the arrowhead is one pixel above or below the last pixel, indicating up or down.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1354760211/10/des.md:165:  - For a vertical body, the arrowhead is one pixel left or right of the last pixel, indicating left or right.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1354760211/10/des.md:166:- Arrows do not overlap. There are at least 2 and at most 5 arrows.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1354760211/10/des.md:169:- For each arrow, determine its pointing direction (up, down, left, or right) from the arrowhead position relative to the body.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1354760211/10/des.md:170:- Let L = the body length (number of pixels in the body, not counting the arrowhead).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1354760211/10/des.md:171:- Starting from the arrowhead pixel, trace a path of L pixels in the pointing direction. If the path reaches a grid boundary before L steps, it reflects (bounces): the component of direction perpendicular to the hit boundary reverses (like a billiard ball), and tracing continues for the remaining steps.
