/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1354760211/6/des.md:92:- "Arrow sprites" are small 3-pixel objects shaped like an L (two pixels forming a straight shaft and one pixel at a 90-degree turn forming the arrowhead). The arrow points from the "tail" end (the free end of the shaft) through the shaft toward the "head" pixel (the pixel at the 90-degree bend). This gives exactly one of eight compass directions (N, NE, E, SE, S, SW, W, NW).
